---
title: "Advanced Airway and Shock Management Lab"
code: "EMS-182"
category: "emergency-medical-services"
credits: "1"
prerequisites: []
corequisites:
  - "2026/EMS-181"
prerequisiteNote: "Prerequisite: Current Virginia EMT and CPR certification as approved by the Virginia Office of EMS."
corequisiteNote: "Co-requisite: EMS 181"
---

Examines assessment and management of trauma emergencies as outlined by the National Emergency Medical Service Education Standards (NEMSES) within the Advanced EMT curriculum. Provides students with specific skills related to airway, resuscitation and shock management. Laboratory 2 hours. Total 2 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
